.Dd September 16, 2026
.Dt NDI_HP_REGISTER 9F
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ndi_hp_register ,
.Nm ndi_hp_unregister ,
.Nm ndi_hp_state_change_req ,
.Nm ndi_hp_walk_cn
.Nd register and manage hotplug connections
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/sunndi.h
.In sys/ddi_hp.h
.In sys/ddi_hp_impl.h
.Ft "int"
.Fo ndi_hp_register
.Fa "dev_info_t *dip"
.Fa "ddi_hp_cn_info_t *info_p"
.Fc
.Ft "int"
.Fo ndi_hp_unregister
.Fa "dev_info_t *dip"
.Fa "char *cn_name"
.Fc
.Ft "int"
.Fo ndi_hp_state_change_req
.Fa "dev_info_t *dip"
.Fa "char *cn_name"
.Fa "ddi_hp_cn_state_t state"
.Fa "uint_t flag"
.Fc
.Ft "void"
.Fo ndi_hp_walk_cn
.Fa "dev_info_t *dip"
.Fa "int (*f)(ddi_hp_cn_info_t *, void *)"
.Fa "void *arg"
.Fc
.Sh INTERFACE LEVEL
illumos specific
.Pq Consolidation Private .
.Sh PARAMETERS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Va dip
Nexus owning the connection.
.It Va info_p
Connection information, including a non-null \fBcn_name\fP.
.It Va cn_name
Null-terminated connection name, unique beneath this nexus.
.It Va state
Target \fBddi_hp_cn_state_t\fP supported by the connection.
.It Va flag
\fBDDI_HP_REQ_SYNC\fP or \fBDDI_HP_REQ_ASYNC\fP.
.It Va f
Connection-walk callback.
.It Va arg
Opaque argument passed to the walk callback.
.El
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These functions connect a nexus or hotplug controller driver to the hotplug
framework.
A connection can be a physical connector or a virtual port representing a
child device.
The nexus must provide the hotplug bus operation required by the framework.
.Pp
\fBndi_hp_register()\fP registers the connection described by \fBinfo_p\fP and queries
its initial state through the nexus.
The information structure and connection name are copied.
Other pointers in the structure are not deep-copied; their storage must
remain valid while the connection uses them.
Registering an already registered name succeeds without replacing its
information.
\fBndi_hp_unregister()\fP removes the named connection if its state permits it.
.Pp
\fBndi_hp_state_change_req()\fP requests \fBstate\fP for a named connection.
Use \fBDDI_HP_REQ_SYNC\fP to perform the operation before returning, or
\fBDDI_HP_REQ_ASYNC\fP to queue it on a framework task queue.
The asynchronous path copies the name and holds \fBdip\fP until the queued work
has finished.
Success from that path reports dispatch, not completion of the state change.
.Pp
\fBndi_hp_walk_cn()\fP calls \fBf(info, arg)\fP for each registered connection while
owning the nexus's device-tree critical section.
The callback returns \fBDDI_WALK_CONTINUE\fP to continue or
\fBDDI_WALK_TERMINATE\fP to stop.
The information pointer belongs to the framework and is not a newly allocated
copy.
The callback may unregister the current connection; it must not use that
connection's information afterwards.
.Pp
Synchronous state changes enter the parent's critical section before the
nexus's section.
A caller already holding the nexus must also have entered its parent first
if the parent exists.
This rule also applies to a walk callback that requests a synchronous change.
.Sh CONTEXT
Registration, unregistration, walking, and synchronous state changes
may be called from user or kernel context and may sleep.
Asynchronous requests may also be made from low-level interrupt context.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Registration returns \fBNDI_SUCCESS\fP, \fBNDI_EINVAL\fP, \fBNDI_ENOTSUP\fP,
or \fBNDI_FAILURE\fP.
Unregistration returns \fBNDI_SUCCESS\fP, \fBNDI_EINVAL\fP, \fBNDI_BUSY\fP, or
\fBNDI_FAILURE\fP.
State requests return \fBNDI_EINVAL\fP for invalid arguments or a missing
connection in the synchronous path, and \fBNDI_ENOTSUP\fP without hotplug
bus operations.
Asynchronous dispatch returns \fBNDI_CLAIMED\fP or \fBNDI_NOMEM\fP.
Synchronous handling returns \fBNDI_CLAIMED\fP or \fBNDI_UNCLAIMED\fP according
to the nexus operation result.
\fBNDI_CLAIMED\fP has the same value as \fBNDI_SUCCESS\fP.
The walk function has no return value.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ndi_devi_enter 9F ,
.Xr ndi_hold_devi 9F ,
.Xr sunndi 9F
